                <note rend="inline" type="source">561.333D3/14: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Secretary General of the Third Pan American Coffee Conference</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Aguilar</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1940-06-17">June 17, 1940</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>In response to your letter of June 14, 1940, the Department of State has
                    designated Mr. Paul C. Daniels, Foreign Service Officer, to attend the Third
                    Pan-American Coffee Conference as its observer.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Cordell Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
